" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 16px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p2_text" data-groupid="p2" class="mobile_p1"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 150%;"><strong>A new focus in fashion.</strong> The style industry is paying closer attention to older female consumers—and not just on the runway. In <em>The New York Times</em>, McKinsey’s <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/T/v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0/5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcd5/5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672?__dU__=v0G4RBKTXg2GsTlMa8YbE0npiPHb7Gzq29ujr-mrJsl6bcn0E30HNSquNCCrd1XNAz&__F__=v0fUYvjHMDjRPMSh3tviDHXIoXcPxvDgUUCCPvXMWoX_0JoZLAZABQFzGdi2cn1iU7KJEa5whIrwYtzM-cxLg6GdgN3lCSNbeBc6ui47Q7lVoFLmjwNbDvNYUFCfX81-jKKF7Og39FLdhpZM4ZNQ2HqfoOEskA3iTTt0Dz3knnLqLw7hlM9J2YlFLzYJ-sTnP89BtM4srorE8_hOTnhi618Vc8J1LqEb32_zPTiGHzvf-DH-mU-VHf3o4PBo1dwr-hxMw5fAz_z7_klJdjuOG_8ATUe9sMC4LpKiT8I_3ZV2efudjObivp2dbG56Jy1MiswS7Y2pzVFgLvl0E35ABBkHlmC0z3HOC7anRmeGeNPhxshebKYacafIKDavBtCdOtvJz1YIXf_nXgsSxwAGLdA4nceXB7gOTYDASL_PDZtUvVKu6TQKt0796BEsxhmLo_PoVHFAMpSUivddMfPR_KA1dy3h5GpNqPoIlXCfgA4wBkiEX56YGeiuNNqMOXqneab5H9f7cP4X5O5idML7XOwA==" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="9083257070ed11f188e0b18e1bc5ed00">Gemma D’Auria</a></span> notes that consumers over 50 represent a major share of both current and future spending power, making age inclusivity a potential new lever of growth.<br><br>“<span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/2026/04/19/style/age-women-fashion.html?__hScId__=v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0&__hRlId__=5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcd6&__hDId__=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672&__hSD__=d3d3Lm55dGltZXMuY29t&cid=mgp_opr-eml-alt-pub-mgp-glb--bundle&hlkid=14e31cd8cf074a0f8c244117ba60bbad&hctky=17208988&hdpid=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="403330a070ee11f18fbce119d32f00d8">Why fashion suddenly loves older women</a></span>” [The New York Times, April 19]<br><br><strong>Also read:</strong> “<span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/industries/retail/our-insights/state-of-fashion?__hScId__=v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0&__hRlId__=5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcd7&__hDId__=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-alt-pub-mgp-glb--bundle&hlkid=445d80efde684f4a9151727c5423281d&hctky=17208988&hdpid=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="e93a53f070ed11f18fecdb82d15270a7">The State of Fashion 2026: When the rules change</a></span>”</span></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-009: Paragraph | P2 --> </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-000: Spacer --><section id="1000" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0"> <tbody><tr> <td height="20" align="left" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" style="line-height: 0px; padding: 0px;"><img src="https://images.harmony.epsilon.com/ContentHandler/images?id=3f67ada7-a01e-4c02-ab71-8b46fd3106ae" height="20" style="display: block; height: 20px" border="0" alt=""></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-000: Spacer --> </td></tr><tr><td><table role="presentation" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="640" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="wrap"><tbody><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-009: Paragraph | P2 --><section id="1009" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 16px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p2_text" data-groupid="p2" class="mobile_p1"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 150%;"><strong>Stablecoins face their real payments test.</strong> While stablecoin transaction volumes are often reported in the trillions of dollars, roughly 99 percent of that activity is tied to crypto trading rather than everyday payments, McKinsey’s <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/T/v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0/5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcd8/5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672?__dU__=v0G4RBKTXg2GsTlMa8YbE0npiPHb7Gzq29ujr-mrJsl6bcn0E30HNSquNCCrd1XNAz&__F__=v0fUYvjHMDjRPMSh3tviDHXIoXcPxvDgUUCCPvXMWoX_0JoZLAZABQFzGdi2cn1iU7KJEa5whIrwYtzM-cxLg6GS8oZxjXJyYZ3VnATQQUlWxM1it8jNnQv-n06UX9mQ9cGPO7MKWD0EapA3gM19s0q2fDRer4YVzolFpE-jcjorZyiLu1sgn-fDZ-VpAG8jhDNSQGUlDjIsKZIY7riRSTgEYZvq8d_2vTWHHluoFkO9-Lh98rEr9AV5k9nuRF6iKU8T9E8HzIz1V1dLLifJ0CqUOEFlNcOrCLHsL1M1rknDXBWpVCyY6NEAj9_OitRY6HDZlMh6mMzXhh4_qobPVEpyfKDZ7jLgdEGFfNazxLrbcmaIlyNs1N9HOeaMRioRSuLgUuS1lmE6NZTb4OFTYkNF4kNu9YcGMaMtnnJw51EqaBRV7qQGyE0n_YJAKlUa9YGpCzPlo0-vtvP6CM5LUqCJTUiD36HcCj6egZpkKWPzdKqWJUFo6dOaJA07ic7RkrmdnJJLNMVlm_YB8WxqopKg==" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="9e795d7070ed11f188e0b18e1bc5ed00">Matt Higginson</a></span> tells Bloomberg. Actual payment usage—such as business transactions, remittances, and cross-border transfers—remains relatively small, but the sector is growing rapidly.<br><br>“<span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/news/videos/2026-05-10/why-stablecoins-are-crypto-s-real-payments-test-video?__hScId__=v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0&__hRlId__=5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcd9&__hDId__=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672&__hSD__=d3d3LmJsb29tYmVyZy5jb20=&cid=mgp_opr-eml-alt-pub-mgp-glb--bundle&hlkid=505ec1139f3c4968b02fa4c85263496b&hctky=17208988&hdpid=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="51e3ffa070ee11f18fbce119d32f00d8">Why stablecoins are crypto’s real payments test</a></span>” [Bloomberg, May 10]<br><br><strong>Also read:</strong> “<span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/industries/financial-services/our-insights/stablecoins-in-payments-what-the-raw-transaction-numbers-miss?__hScId__=v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0&__hRlId__=5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcda&__hDId__=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-alt-pub-mgp-glb--bundle&hlkid=6234eb45b59c414db3e5c8a32958541b&hctky=17208988&hdpid=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="f90dd77070ed11f18fecdb82d15270a7">Stablecoins in payments: What the raw transaction numbers miss</a></span>”</span></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-009: Paragraph | P2 --> </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-000: Spacer --><section id="1000" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0"> <tbody><tr> <td height="20" align="left" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" style="line-height: 0px; padding: 0px;"><img src="https://images.harmony.epsilon.com/ContentHandler/images?id=3f67ada7-a01e-4c02-ab71-8b46fd3106ae" height="20" style="display: block; height: 20px" border="0" alt=""></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-000: Spacer --> </td></tr><tr><td><table role="presentation" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="640" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="wrap"><tbody><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-009: Paragraph | P2 --><section id="1009" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 16px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p2_text" data-groupid="p2" class="mobile_p1"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 150%;"><strong>The human–AI workforce is here.</strong> As AI agents take on a larger share of work, McKinsey’s <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/T/v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0/5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcdb/5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672?__dU__=v0G4RBKTXg2GsTlMa8YbE0npiPHb7Gzq29ujr-mrJsl6bcn0E30HNSquNCCrd1XNAz&__F__=v0fUYvjHMDjRPMSh3tviDHXIoXcPxvDgUUCCPvXMWoX_0JoZLAZABQFzGdi2cn1iU7KJEa5whIrwYtzM-cxLg6Gf0e1atU0hcdCjFcgr95w7QFLmjwNbDvNYUFCfX81-jKKF7Og39FLdhpZM4ZNQ2HqfoOEskA3iTTt0Dz3knnLqLw7hlM9J2YlFLzYJ-sTnP89BtM4srorE8_hOTnhi618Vc8J1LqEb32_zPTiGHzvf-DH-mU-VHf3uENATjgE6CHmYx9Jh0Sm41mGyMYaxI9tw7vTNFqM3q36bfkTd0ciqKfudjObivp2dbG56Jy1MiswS7Y2pzVFgLvl0E35ABBkHlmC0z3HOC7anRmeGeNPhxshebKYacafIKDavBtCdOtvJz1YIXf_nXgsSxwAGLdA4nceXB7gOTYDASL_PDZtUvVKu6TQKt0796BEsxhmLo_PoVHFAMpSUjKXpqzUTS6Fxzj3UgpYeVSd5U96sDKAjE5OlaZgLPbiAMr_gdrQi9Kb5H9f7cP4X5O5idML7XOwA==" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="af5465e070ed11f188e0b18e1bc5ed00">Anu Madgavkar</a></span> points to a future in which leaders must redesign work around human and machine collaboration. Madgavkar tells Fortune that 30 to 50 percent of a person’s work hours and activities could transform in the next three to five years. That means the question is no longer just which tasks AI can perform, but how organizations prepare people to work alongside technology.<br><br>“<span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/2026/05/21/mckinsey-partner-anu-madgavkar-50-work-hours-could-be-transformed-within-next-5-years/?__hScId__=v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0&__hRlId__=5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcdc&__hDId__=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672&__hSD__=Zm9ydHVuZS5jb20=&cid=mgp_opr-eml-alt-pub-mgp-glb--bundle&hlkid=740d83dfa5d94f1382c9cf437536ada3&hctky=17208988&hdpid=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="6569679070ee11f18fbce119d32f00d8">McKinsey partner says up to 50% of work hours could be transformed within the next five years</a></span>” [Fortune, May 21]<br><br><strong>Also read:</strong> “<span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/capabilities/people-and-organizational-performance/our-insights/the-rise-of-the-human-ai-workforce?__hScId__=v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0&__hRlId__=5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcdd&__hDId__=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672&__hSD__=d3d3Lm1ja2luc2V5LmNvbQ==&cid=mgp_opr-eml-alt-pub-mgp-glb--bundle&hlkid=f4d6818ac9b8463bbaa9a35019e68bf0&hctky=17208988&hdpid=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="09ac4c1070ee11f18fecdb82d15270a7">The rise of the human–AI workforce</a></span>”</span></p></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-009: Paragraph | P2 --> </td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-000: Spacer --><section id="1000" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0"> <tbody><tr> <td height="20" align="left" valign="top" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" style="line-height: 0px; padding: 0px;"><img src="https://images.harmony.epsilon.com/ContentHandler/images?id=3f67ada7-a01e-4c02-ab71-8b46fd3106ae" height="20" style="display: block; height: 20px" border="0" alt=""></td> </tr> </tbody></table> </td> </tr> </tbody></table> </div> </section> <!-- End 1-000: Spacer --> </td></tr><tr><td><table role="presentation" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" width="640" border="0" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="wrap"><tbody><tr><td bgcolor="#FFFFFF"><!-- Start 1-009: Paragraph | P2 --><section id="1009" layout-row="true"><div layout-row="true"><table layout-row="true" role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF"> <tbody><tr layout-row="true"> <td valign="top" align="left"> <table role="presentation" width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" class="wrap"> <tbody><tr> <td align="left" style="padding: 0px 20px 16px 20px" class="pad20rl match"><p style="font-size: 14px; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; line-height: 150%; margin: 0px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: 0px; text-transform: none; color: #333333; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif" enable-personalization="true" data-richtext="p2_text" data-groupid="p2" class="mobile_p1"><span style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 150%;"><strong>African banking turns a corner.</strong> The continent’s banking sector has crossed a new threshold, McKinsey Partner <span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/T/v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0/5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcde/5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672?__dU__=v0G4RBKTXg2GsTlMa8YbE0npiPHb7Gzq29ujr-mrJsl6bcn0E30HNSquNCCrd1XNAz&__F__=v0fUYvjHMDjRPMSh3tviDHXIoXcPxvDgUUCCPvXMWoX_0JoZLAZABQFzGdi2cn1iU7KJEa5whIrwYtzM-cxLg6GQNx0qj7ir5aGbKrC0gyt2QFLmjwNbDvNYUFCfX81-jKKF7Og39FLdhpZM4ZNQ2HqfoOEskA3iTTt0Dz3knnLqLw7hlM9J2YlFLzYJ-sTnP89BtM4srorE8_hOTnhi618Vc8J1LqEb32_zPTiGHzvf-DH-mU-VHf3uTHQe-_ig7e7XzFHm2Z1B_o_r6o3iwk7R12q0_Uosrl-G-sanEUl8GfudjObivp2dbG56Jy1MiswS7Y2pzVFgLvl0E35ABBkHlmC0z3HOC7anRmeGeNPhxshebKYacafIKDavBtCdOtvJz1YIXf_nXgsSxwAGLdA4nceXB7gOTYDASL_PDZtUvVKu6TQKt0796BEsxhmLo_PoVHFAMpSUgvJFnhkn0tJNTnYwJxK0iBpghSKkG_MYgjMfudOFI1-wk6Axiavc65b5H9f7cP4X5O5idML7XOwA==" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="ca96da4070ed11f188e0b18e1bc5ed00">Mayowa Kuyoro</a></span> tells Reuters, moving “from a story of potential to one of performance,” with revenues topping $100 billion for the first time and returns well above the global average. The next challenge is turning that momentum into durable growth, as banks scale digital capabilities, move beyond traditional lending, and navigate currency volatility and concentrated revenue pools.<br><br>“<span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/world/africa/african-banks-outpace-global-peers-returns-revenues-top-100-billion-mckinsey-2026-03-31/?__hScId__=v710000019f0b1dcd77c67fa4f4bbe5cfc0&__hRlId__=5f9d887ec4fa44210000021ef3a0bcdf&__hDId__=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672&__hSD__=d3d3LnJldXRlcnMuY29t&cid=mgp_opr-eml-alt-pub-mgp-glb--bundle&hlkid=05ee5c3f9ae94a71919c6b1b08cc6c89&hctky=17208988&hdpid=5f9d887e-c4fa-4421-8c1d-4fef732a7672" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: rgb(34, 81, 255); font-weight: inherit; background: none; text-decoration: underline;" data-link-id="775e929070ee11f18fbce119d32f00d8">African banks outpace global peers on returns as revenues top $100 billion, McKinsey says</a></span>” [Reuters, March 31]<br><br><strong>Also read:</strong> “<span style="text-decoration: underline; line-height: 150%; color: rgb(34, 81, 255);"><a href="https://email.mckinsey.com/industries/financial-services/our-insights/from-potential-to-perf